<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/19/eng@/~cl_4> <https://schema.org/name> "The principal Act is amended by inserting after Part VII"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/19/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/19/eng@/~cl_4> <https://schema.org/text> "the following Part: \" PART VIIA EXTENSION OF THE FUNCTIONS, ETC., OF THE PORT AUTHORITY TO OTHER PORTS 66A. (1) The Minister may, by order published in the Gazette, extend the functions, powers, duties and jurisdiction of the Authority to other ports. (2) An order under subsection (1) may provide that the Authority shall, in carrying out the administration of the port to which its control is extended, include among its members such other person or persons as may be specified in the order either by name or by office. (3) Where an order is made under subsection (1), the Authority shall be deemed for all purposes to be the port authority in respect of the port specified in the order as if it were a port authority established in respect of that port under this Act and shall in carrying out its functions be styled by such name as may be provided in the order. The 66B. The Authority in carrying out its functions in authority respect of the port to which they are extended shall in carrying carry them out as if it were an independent port out its extended authority established in respect of such port. functions shall be deemed to be an independent port authority. Power of 66c. An order of the Minister under section 66A Minister may contain all such provisions as the Minister may to make provisions deem necessary to enable the Authority to carry out for the its functions in relation to the port to which they are Authority extended. to carry out its functions. Inter- 66D. For the purposes of this Part, \"port\" means a pretation. Federal port or a place declared to be a Federal port by Federal law.\"."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1995/19/eng@> .
